# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sentinel — Environment Variables
#
# As of the agent/server split, configuration is per-package:
#
#   server/.env.example   — control plane: auth, DB, agent connection
#   agent/.env.example    — privileged host agent: host paths, Docker
#                            socket, managed services allowlist
#
# Copy each to server/.env and agent/.env respectively and fill in
# your values. This root-level file is kept only as a pointer — it is
# not read directly by either process.
#
# Once the native installer (Phase 2) exists, these become generated
# by `sentinel install` into /etc/sentinel/ rather than hand-edited.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
